WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.113 --> 00:00:01.899
- Right after I proposed to her, she goes,

00:00:01.899 --> 00:00:04.647
I wanna take a picture with
my new ring on in the ocean.

00:00:04.647 --> 00:00:06.336
- You know, social
media wants that moment.

00:00:06.336 --> 00:00:07.283
- That was not the moment

00:00:07.283 --> 00:00:09.483
where the ring got lost, thank goodness.

00:00:09.483 --> 00:00:12.675
(Classical music)

00:00:12.675 --> 00:00:13.508
- I proposed.

00:00:13.508 --> 00:00:15.066
- Well, 'cause I was begging for years.

00:00:15.066 --> 00:00:17.603
- It was back and forth
for the last three years.

00:00:17.603 --> 00:00:19.723
It was cheaper to get married than

00:00:19.723 --> 00:00:22.817
to buy another plane
ticket, so here we are.

00:00:22.817 --> 00:00:23.960
- And also, he loves me.

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:24.988
- And also, I love her.

00:00:24.988 --> 00:00:26.605
- It was on New Year's
Eve when I proposed.

00:00:26.605 --> 00:00:28.451
- We were only seven months into dating.

00:00:28.451 --> 00:00:29.654
Nobody was pregnant.

00:00:29.654 --> 00:00:33.214
- We got to spend our first
week of marriage sleeping

00:00:33.214 --> 00:00:37.823
in a small tent and so, that
was kind of our adventure.

00:00:37.823 --> 00:00:38.779
- Who lost the ring and how
- Molly

00:00:38.779 --> 00:00:39.795
- [Narrator] did that all happen?

00:00:39.795 --> 00:00:40.767
- Molly lost the ring.

00:00:40.767 --> 00:00:42.520
- Okay, it was stolen.

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:44.255
- It was not stolen.

00:00:44.255 --> 00:00:46.503
- I asked my aunt if I could have

00:00:46.503 --> 00:00:49.365
my grandmother's wedding
ring to give to Jackie.

00:00:49.365 --> 00:00:51.190
She was like, put the
ring in your backpack.

00:00:51.190 --> 00:00:52.531
She said to me, right, Jamie,

00:00:52.531 --> 00:00:55.444
I'm gonna give you this ring,
but please don't lose it.

00:00:55.444 --> 00:00:59.004
- The first ring, I ended up
being allergic to the metal.

00:00:59.004 --> 00:01:01.810
- I'd taken the old ring,
and I went and exchanged it

00:01:01.810 --> 00:01:05.385
and bought a really nice traditional ring.

00:01:05.385 --> 00:01:08.285
- I wasn't allergic to
the metal of that one.

00:01:08.285 --> 00:01:11.017
I was allergic to the style of that one.

00:01:11.017 --> 00:01:12.953
- I was living with my roommate Erin

00:01:12.953 --> 00:01:16.586
and I was watching her dogs
because she was out of town.

00:01:16.586 --> 00:01:19.454
Put it next to my bed and in
the morning, it was not there.

00:01:19.454 --> 00:01:21.312
And I look at these sweet dogs,

00:01:21.312 --> 00:01:23.401
and they weren't so sweet anymore.

00:01:23.401 --> 00:01:25.201
- I put it in my gym bag, safe.

00:01:25.201 --> 00:01:28.417
Did a really hard work
out, yes, I'm amazing.

00:01:28.417 --> 00:01:31.667
Go back to the gym bag and it was gone.

00:01:32.893 --> 00:01:34.553
My ring was the showpiece.

00:01:34.553 --> 00:01:37.163
It was rose gold, diamond band.

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:39.110
- Stop, it hurts me
- with a big rock.

00:01:39.110 --> 00:01:40.874
- to hear you talk about it.

00:01:40.874 --> 00:01:44.396
- Got on the train, put my
bag next to me, fell asleep.

00:01:44.396 --> 00:01:46.971
And then I heard the
announcer announce my stop.

00:01:46.971 --> 00:01:48.537
And I jumped off of the train,

00:01:48.537 --> 00:01:51.012
went up the escalators, and
it was when I got to the top

00:01:51.012 --> 00:01:53.387
that I realized I didn't have my bag

00:01:53.387 --> 00:01:55.181
which had the wedding ring.

00:01:55.181 --> 00:01:56.747
- So I don't know who has my wedding ring

00:01:56.747 --> 00:01:57.781
but I hope they're enjoying it.

00:01:57.781 --> 00:01:59.011
- But it's not her, yeah.

00:01:59.011 --> 00:02:01.652
- For and a half days, was going through

00:02:01.652 --> 00:02:03.892
all the poop of these dogs,

00:02:03.892 --> 00:02:05.937
really feeling the hotness of it

00:02:05.937 --> 00:02:07.572
and I could not find this ring.

00:02:07.572 --> 00:02:10.187
And then I look in between
my bed and my bedside table

00:02:10.187 --> 00:02:12.135
and my ring is wedged in between.

00:02:12.135 --> 00:02:14.115
- I had no idea that this even happened.

00:02:14.115 --> 00:02:18.260
- I took it off to shower
and it fell down the sink.

00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:19.773
- Then you have to call
the whole plumber thing,

00:02:19.773 --> 00:02:23.918
and then he was searching
for it, couldn't find it.

00:02:23.918 --> 00:02:25.950
You said it fell down
the sink or the shower?

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:28.450
- The sink, the bathroom sink.

00:02:30.135 --> 00:02:31.666
- Okay, did you lose that ring?

00:02:31.666 --> 00:02:32.524
Did you not lose that ring?

00:02:32.524 --> 00:02:33.357
- It's gone.

00:02:33.357 --> 00:02:34.333
- Obviously, it's gone,
but did you lose it?

00:02:34.333 --> 00:02:36.196
- I don't know where it is.

00:02:36.196 --> 00:02:37.029
- Anna.

00:02:37.029 --> 00:02:39.446
- I don't know where it went.

00:02:40.819 --> 00:02:42.312
- Well, whatever, I mean, she's my wife.

00:02:42.312 --> 00:02:44.385
I love her to death, so no matter

00:02:44.385 --> 00:02:47.711
if I gotta buy a ring every year.

00:02:47.711 --> 00:02:50.544
(classical music)

00:02:53.855 --> 00:02:55.308
- Ooh.

00:02:55.308 --> 00:02:57.971
- Please tell me my
lost ring isn't in here.

00:02:57.971 --> 00:02:59.404
- Yeah, right?

00:02:59.404 --> 00:03:01.476
- This one's pretty, it
looks like my actual ring.

00:03:01.476 --> 00:03:03.670
- I like, you can stack these, look.

00:03:03.670 --> 00:03:04.791
- I think this would be awesome for

00:03:04.791 --> 00:03:07.160
working out and stuff 'cause I
always leave my ring at home.

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:08.605
- They make me wanna go rock climbing.

00:03:08.605 --> 00:03:10.588
- After I'd lost my ring, I was panicking.

00:03:10.588 --> 00:03:12.128
So I causally throw out the,

00:03:12.128 --> 00:03:13.661
hey, we should get these Qalo rings.

00:03:13.661 --> 00:03:17.078
- This is the most fun I've had all week.

